export const meta = {
  name: 'wave3-i18n-extract',
  description: 'Wave 3: extract and translate client texts in 7 parallel chunks (each reviewed adversarially and fixed)',
  phases: [{ title: 'Extract' }, { title: 'Review' }, { title: 'Fix' }],
}
const SP = 'C:\\Users\\akitl\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--travaille-godot-towermoulineux2\\7020066a-783a-415a-a50d-d8623080aee1\\scratchpad\\'
const ENV = `
ENVIRONMENT OF THIS MACHINE (overrides the paths written in CLAUDE.md, which come from another machine):
- Main repo: C:\\travaille\\godot\\towermoulineux2, integration branch 'v1' (HEAD 612caa3 or later: waves 1-2 merged + shared translations). In your OWN git worktree: it may have been created from master — first run \`git switch -c <your branch> && git reset --hard v1\` and check \`git log -1 v1\`. Commit only on your branch (Conventional Commits in English with scope, e.g. "feat(godot): translate the <chunk> texts", ending with "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"). Never push, never touch remotes, never edit docs/v1/*, CLAUDE.md, project.godot, godot/i18n/common.csv or another chunk's CSV.
- Godot 4.7.2 ONLY: headless /c/travaille/godot/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64_console.exe ; windowed: /c/travaille/godot/Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64.exe. Fresh worktree: run \`$G --headless --path godot --import\` TWICE (first may log missing .translation files or crash transiently). After editing a CSV, re-import before running tests. Baseline on v1: 803 tests pass, lint 0 WARNING.
- Tests: \`LHT_TEST_HTTP_PORT=<your port> $G --headless --path godot --script res://tests/run_tests.gd\` (0 failed; add \`-- --filter=<name>\` to narrow). Lint: \`$G --headless -d --path godot --script res://tests/check_scripts.gd < /dev/null\` (0 WARNING).
- Temp: $TEMP/lht-<your branch>/. Stop processes you start by PID only. No Go/C++ changes in this wave.`

const RULES = `
I18N RULES (foundation already merged; read godot/core/i18n/{tx,lht_locale,plural_rules,number_style}.gd, godot/i18n/common.csv, godot/tests/core/i18n/*, godot/tests/support/i18n_csv.gd, settings_panel.gd for the refresh pattern):
- msgid = the CURRENT French text, byte-identical (NBSP, « », ellipsis…), so the ~600 French test assertions stay true WITHOUT modifying existing tests. The French output of every function must stay identical (tests run pinned to fr).
- Use Tx.t(msgid), Tx.f(msgid, {name: value}) for named params, Tx.n("{n} tour|{n} tours", count, args) for plurals. Convert "%s"/"%d" formats into named placeholders ({titan}, {time}, {n}…) — never "%s" in a msgid. Replace every \`"s" if n > 1\` plural hack by Tx.n. Never build a sentence by concatenating fragments: make whole msgids (test_translations_complete rejects leading/trailing spaces). Keep separators (" · ") in code only when they are pure punctuation.
- const tables of French texts stay French msgids; translate at use (Tx.t(TABLE[k])). Comparisons must keep comparing msgids/ids, never translated text (e.g. \`spawned == WORLD_TITAN_FALLBACK\`, \`label.text != done_text\`).
- Server texts are NEVER translated: catalog names (buildings, towers, titans, items, hunts), server error messages (error.message fallback), player names. A Label whose text is set in code (via Tx or with server data) gets \`auto_translate_mode = Node.AUTO_TRANSLATE_MODE_DISABLED\` (in .tscn or code), otherwise a catalog name equal to a msgid ("Atelier", "Dégâts", "Portée", "Cadence", "Neutre", "Hutte du chasseur") would be translated.
- Static .tscn texts (text =, tooltip_text =, placeholder_text =) are auto-translated: their msgids must be in a table (yours, or common.csv).
- Every scene script that writes text in code re-renders on language change: \`func _notification(what: int) -> void: if what == NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED and is_node_ready(): <existing _refresh()/_render()>\`. Toasts already shown keep their language (accepted).
- Numbers: use StatFormat / NumberStyle (core/presentation/stat_format.gd, core/i18n/number_style.gd), TimeUtil.format_duration; dates as a reorderable msgid like "{day}/{month}/{year}".
- Do NOT change the signature of a public function used outside your paths (other chunks are being converted in parallel); add a new function if needed and keep the old one working.
- Your CSV: godot/i18n/<chunk>.csv (header keys,en,es,de,ja,ko,zh,pt,ru; RFC CSV quoting; keep its existing seed row unless obsolete). Fill ALL 8 languages for every msgid. NEVER add a row whose msgid is already in godot/i18n/common.csv (use it as is). Plural rows: forms separated by "|": en/es/de/pt 2, ru 4 (one|few|many|other), ja/ko/zh 1. Placeholders identical to the msgid's.
- Translation quality: follow ${SP}glossary.csv (188 terms: use them EXACTLY) and ${SP}i18n_style.md (register, typography, quotes, plural counters). Terminology from LHT1 (C:\\travaille\\godot\\towermoulineux\\client\\ressources\\trad\\trad.csv). Real, idiomatic game-UI translations — no machine-literal calques, no English left in other columns. NEVER the word replay/rejeu or any equivalent in any language (§17 — the style guide lists them); "Réessayer" = retry.
