- Every scene script that writes text in code re-renders on language change: \`func _notification(what: int) -> void: if what == NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED and is_node_ready(): <existing _refresh()/_render()>\`. Toasts already shown keep their language (accepted).
- Numbers: use StatFormat / NumberStyle (core/presentation/stat_format.gd, core/i18n/number_style.gd), TimeUtil.format_duration; dates as a reorderable msgid like "{day}/{month}/{year}".
- Do NOT change the signature of a public function used outside your paths (other chunks are being converted in parallel); add a new function if needed and keep the old one working.
- Your CSV: godot/i18n/<chunk>.csv (header keys,en,es,de,ja,ko,zh,pt,ru; RFC CSV quoting; keep its existing seed row unless obsolete). Fill ALL 8 languages for every msgid. NEVER add a row whose msgid is already in godot/i18n/common.csv (use it as is). Plural rows: forms separated by "|": en/es/de/pt 2, ru 4 (one|few|many|other), ja/ko/zh 1. Placeholders identical to the msgid's.
- Translation quality: follow ${SP}glossary.csv (188 terms: use them EXACTLY) and ${SP}i18n_style.md (register, typography, quotes, plural counters). Terminology from LHT1 (C:\\travaille\\godot\\towermoulineux\\client\\ressources\\trad\\trad.csv). Real, idiomatic game-UI translations — no machine-literal calques, no English left in other columns. NEVER the word replay/rejeu or any equivalent in any language (§17 — the style guide lists them); "Réessayer" = retry.
- Per-chunk hints and traps: ${SP}i18n_shared.md (read the section for your chunk and the general traps).
- New French texts added by waves 1-2 that must be covered (in whichever chunk owns the file): toasts « Bâtiment amélioré : {building}, niveau {level}. » / « Bâtiment construit : {building}. »; « Construction… »/« Amélioration… »; « Tours posées : N », « W × H cases », « Votre grille s'agrandit : W × H. », HUD tooltip « Nombre de tours posées sur la grille de défense. »; HP percent and reward markers (HpBarModel/SegmentedHpBar/CombatHud), « Voir le combat »; « Disposition verrouillée pendant le combat. », « Planifier la défense sur le parchemin (touche P). », « Un combat est en cours : lancez le suivant après « Continuer ». », « Posée dans la défense : elle ne peut rien recevoir pendant le combat en cours. ».
- Add godot/tests/core/i18n/test_<chunk>_i18n.gd: every msgid held in your const tables exists in a table; a few rendered texts with parameters and plurals checked in 'en' and 'ru' (set the locale in the test and restore 'fr' after, like the existing i18n tests); one scene of yours re-renders on NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED (switch to 'de', check a text changed, back to 'fr'). Do not edit test_tx_sources.gd (shared) — but make sure it passes (it scans Tx literals).
- Commit the new .uid files of new scripts. DONE = full run_tests 0 failed, lint 0 WARNING, i18n tests green, worktree clean.`

const CHUNKS = [
  { key: 'shell', paths: 'godot/core/app, godot/core/session (EXCEPT profile_settings.gd and settings_applier.gd), godot/core/input, godot/core/catalog, godot/core/util (EXCEPT time_util.gd), godot/core/camera, godot/scenes/menu, godot/scenes/boot, godot/scenes/ui (EXCEPT settings/ and hp_bar/), godot/scenes/scene_router.gd, runtime godot/art/** scripts (not art/tests or art tools)' },
  { key: 'net_notify', paths: 'godot/core/notify, godot/core/net, godot/core/services, godot/core/sync, godot/core/state, godot/core/autoload (EXCEPT session.gd)' },
  { key: 'world', paths: 'godot/core/world, godot/scenes/world, godot/scenes/hud, godot/scenes/valley (NB: WorldText.hp_total prints "300 PV" with a regular space — use your own msgid "{hp} PV" with a normal space, not the NBSP one of common.csv)' },
  { key: 'village_core', paths: 'godot/core/village (NB: VillageText.countdown should use the common templates "Prêt dans {time}" / "De nouveau disponible dans {time}" — keep its current signature working for scenes/village callers)' },
  { key: 'village_ui', paths: 'godot/scenes/village (all panels, village_module, hut, merchant, workshop, temple, hq…)' },
  { key: 'combat', paths: 'godot/core/encounter, godot/scenes/combat (incl. scenes/combat/ui/combat_hud.*), godot/scenes/ui/hp_bar' },
  { key: 'planning', paths: 'godot/core/planning, godot/scenes/planning, godot/core/domain, godot/core/presentation (EXCEPT stat_format.gd; includes hp_bar_model.gd and valley_text.gd)' },
]
const IMPL_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', properties: {
  branch: { type: 'string' }, worktree_path: { type: 'string' }, commits: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  msgids_added: { type: 'number' }, summary: { type: 'string' }, tests: { type: 'string' },
  decisions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, open_issues: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } },
  required: ['branch', 'worktree_path', 'commits', 'msgids_added', 'summary', 'tests', 'decisions', 'open_issues'] }
const REVIEW_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', properties: { issues: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {
  severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] }, file: { type: 'string' }, description: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } },
  required: ['severity', 'file', 'description', 'evidence'] } } }, required: ['issues'] }
const FIX_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', properties: { fixed: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, rejected: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, commits: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, tests: { type: 'string' } }, required: ['fixed', 'rejected', 'commits', 'tests'] }

const results = await pipeline(CHUNKS.map((c, i) => ({ ...c, port: 18080 + i, rport: 18087 + i, branch: `v1-w3-i18n-${c.key}` })),
  c => agent(`You implement branch ${c.branch} of the LHT2 Godot client: extract and translate every player-visible text of the "${c.key}" chunk into the 8 other languages (wave 3 of the i18n plan, user decision: 9 languages fr,en,es,de,ja,ko,zh,pt,ru, client only, you produce the translations).
YOUR PATHS (modify only these, plus godot/i18n/${c.key}.csv and your new test godot/tests/core/i18n/test_${c.key}_i18n.gd; touch existing tests only if a French output had to change, which should not happen): ${c.paths}.
First list every player-visible French literal in your paths (grep .gd and .tscn for text/tooltip_text and string literals; LhtLog/debug strings and identifiers are NOT player text), then convert, then translate.
YOUR PORT: LHT_TEST_HTTP_PORT=${c.port}.
${RULES}
${ENV}
Return the structured report (worktree_path = absolute path of your worktree; msgids_added = rows added to your CSV).`, { label: `extract:${c.key}`, phase: 'Extract', isolation: 'worktree', schema: IMPL_SCHEMA }),
  (impl, c) => {
    if (!impl) return null
    return agent(`Adversarial reviewer of i18n branch ${impl.branch} (chunk "${c.key}", paths: ${c.paths}) in worktree ${impl.worktree_path}. Read \`git -C "${impl.worktree_path}" diff v1...HEAD\` and the owned files in context. Try to REFUTE that the chunk is complete and correct:
(1) player-visible French left untranslated in the owned paths (grep accented and unaccented literals, .tscn texts not in any CSV, tooltips, placeholder texts, plural hacks left, concatenated fragments);
(2) correctness: French output changed (tests pinned to fr must be unchanged), placeholder/plural bugs, comparisons now on translated text, server/catalog names passed through Tx or auto-translated (auto_translate_mode missing on code-set labels), missing NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED refresh, public signature changes used outside the paths;
