  tofu boxes, no French left in client texts (the French that remains is server names and descriptions, by design). Some captures (the remaining world and village views in ja, ru and de) were produced and their capture runs reported OK, but I did not look at them closely.
INT tests "Run headless with Godot 4.7.2 and LHT_TEST_HTTP_PORT=18080:
- run_tests.gd: 859 passed, 0 failed, 0 broken (start: 846);
- check_scripts.gd (-d): 415 scripts compiled, 0 WARNING;
- art_checks.gd: ART_CHECKS_OK (7676 checks).

New or extended tests:
- tests/project/test_i18n_live_switch.gd (7 tests);
- tests/project/test_no_hardcoded_french.gd (3 tests, scanner self-test included);
- tests/core/i18n/test_number_style.gd::test_the_rate_unit_agrees_with_the_rate;
- tests/scenes/village/test_village_panel_fit.gd::test_every_village_panel_stays_in_its_area_in_every_language_{ru_de_es_pt,en_ja_ko_zh}.

Go was not touched, so the Go tests were not run."
INT decisions ["D-391 · 2026-10-15 · client · Fire rate unit: StatFormat.RATE_TEXT becomes the plural msgid "{value} tir/s|{value} tir/s" (French unit invariable, French output unchanged), formatted by Tx.n on the displayed (rounded to 0.01) rate. en "1 shot/s" / "1.5 shots/s", es and pt "disparo/s" / "disparos/s" (pt: singular below 2), de "Schuss/s" (invariable), ru "выстр./с" in all 4 forms, ja/ko/zh unchanged. The common row "{value} tir/s" is replaced. Rejected: a unit without a noun ("{value}/s"), and the French plural "tirs/s", which would change French output.","D-392 · 2026-10-15 · tests · Guard against French without a translation: test_no_hardcoded_french scans core/ and scenes/. A French literal (accented letter or « ») is a Tx msgid, a msgid constant, a developer message (LhtLog, push_*, print, assert), a text of the parchment's auto-translated nodes (still a CSV msgid), or a commented exception (endonyms, a countdown lookup key, invalid_response details, logged-only launch warnings, an ignored quarantine message). Every text, tooltip_text and placeholder_text that a .tscn has the engine translate must be a CSV msgid. Accent-based, so unaccented French ("Toutes", "Lecture impossible…") falls outside it; a manual scan found no such leftover shown to the player.","D-393 · 2026-10-15 · tests · Live language switch: test_i18n_live_switch switches the main screens fr -> de -> en and requires no German left, no French msgid unchanged between de and en (except the collisions of catalog names: Marchand, Atelier, Hutte du chasseur, Temple des Titans, QG, Neutre, and the Dégâts/Portée/Cadence modifiers), and English texts. Comparisons go by text, not by node path, because the rebuilt reports and cards recreate their nodes.","D-394 · 2026-10-15 · client · The village module sends the hut's refusal (LaunchLock: fight shown, world visit) again on NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED, like combat_module does for its panels.","D-395 · 2026-10-15 · client · Fitting translations into 1280x720 panels at 125 %: the hunt card's bait/button row becomes an HFlowContainer (the button goes under the bait only when both do not fit; French layout unchanged). Shorter translations: de "Kaufen & öffnen", ru "Купить" (Acheter et ouvrir); ja "配置（{x}, {y}）", "{placement} · 補正込み"; ru "{placement} · с бонусами". test_village_panel_fit runs every village panel in the 8 other languages at 1280x720 and 125 %.","D-396 · 2026-10-15 · tools · capture.gd --lang=<code>: language applied as the settings do (locale and font fallbacks) and pinned as the system language, so the capture stages' temporary profiles keep it; applied again around each capture_set_view. Review: --resolutions=1280x720 on menu, village, combat, world and valley_review (parchment, tower card)."]
INT open_issues ["For the orchestrator (STATUS.md, wave 5.4): record the live switch, the no-French guard, the windowed captures in ja, ru and de, and the green counts (859 / 0 WARNING / ART_CHECKS_OK). Add D-391 to D-396 to DECISIONS.md. CONTRACTS.md: nothing to change. The README for the capture tool could mention --lang (it is documented in capture.gd's header).","Cosmetic: in ja, ko and zh, labels in Alegreya or Cinzel (panel subtitles "レベル₁", fusion slots "タワー₁") take their digits from Alegreya's old-style figures while the kana come from the Noto fallback, so the digits look like subscripts. It reads correctly, with no tofu. Possible fix: lining figures (OpenType 'lnum') on the Alegreya variations, or Inter for these labels in CJK.","Server texts stay French in every language by design (building and titan names, building descriptions, lore, catalog modifiers and rarities such as « Peu commune », « Épique »). The captures show the language mix on every panel. If the product wants these translated, it needs a localized server catalog, which is outside V1.","test_no_hardcoded_french only detects accented French or « »; it cannot see unaccented French. A one-off rough scan found no unaccented leftover shown to the player.","Text already shown keeps its language after a switch, by design (D-389): toasts, announcements, status lines, errors. The live switch test does not cover those overlays."]

