[
 {
  "lens": "i18n",
  "issues": [
   {
    "severity": "medium",
    "file": "godot/core/notify/error_messages.gd",
    "description": "Several server error codes that a player can actually hit are missing from ErrorMessages._ERRORS. describe() then falls back to the server's French message, so these errors show in French in all 9 languages. The missing codes are engine_unavailable (fight launch while the sim is down, a 503), invalid_steam_ticket (boot sign-in in Steam mode, which goes through BootSequence._sign_in_message -> describe), visit_not_found and no_active_titan (world engagement races), insufficient_items (workshop transfer), encounter_not_found, player_not_found and balance_overflow. Server texts staying French is by design, but the client's code table exists to translate the codes the player can see, and these codes are absent from it.",
    "evidence": "Codes that the server emits (grep of apperr.<Kind>(\"code\", ...) in serveur/internal) minus the keys of _ERRORS gives: balance_overflow, duplicate_tower*, encounter_not_found, engine_unavailable, insufficient_items, invalid_loadout*, invalid_steam_ticket, no_active_titan, no_announced_visit (dev console), not_found, player_not_found, steam_unavailable*, test_refused, tower_not_found*, visit_not_found (* = handled elsewhere in the client). Examples: serveur/internal/sim/runner.go:46 ErrUnavailable = apperr.Unavailable(\"engine_unavailable\", \"Le moteur de combat est momentanément indisponible, réessayez.\"); serveur/internal/auth/service.go:51 apperr.Unauthenticated(\"invalid_steam_ticket\", \"Ticket Steam refusé.\"); serveur/internal/world/world.go:101,103. error_messages.gd describe(): `if _ERRORS.has(error.code): return Tx.t(...)` / `if not error.message.is_empty(): return error.message`, so in en or ja the toast or boot error reads e.g. « Le moteur de combat est momentanément indisponible, réessayez. »."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "godot/scenes/hud/hud.gd",
    "description": "During a fight (HUD values frozen, §17), a language change does not rewrite the HUD resource values. The MSQ tier label stays in the old language (« Palier 2 » after fr -> de -> en), and gold keeps the old language's grouping (« 1 250 » instead of « 1,250 »), until the fight presentation ends. The cause is _refresh_texts(), which calls _refresh_all() only when `not _frozen`. The frozen numbers are not kept apart, so they cannot be re-rendered. This permanent HUD element is not one of the D-389 categories that keep their language (toast, announcement, status line, error). The live-switch test covers the valley HUD only outside a fight.",
    "evidence": "Headless probe on a copy of the branch (stage res://tests/scenes/village/village_capture_stage.tscn, view fight_merchant: a main-quest fight followed from the Village with the Merchant open). The probe built the stage in fr, switched de then en the way Settings does (LhtLocale.apply + LhtFonts.follow_language), then dumped the visible texts. Result: `VillageCaptureStage/Valley/HudLayer/Hud/Resources/.../Tier  label  Palier 2` and `.../Gold  label  1 250`. Built directly in en, the same shot shows `Stage 2` and `1,250`. It reproduces the same way in ja (ステージ2 expected), ru (Этап 2) and pt (Etapa 2). Every other capture-stage shot (menu, village, world, combat, valley_review) has identical texts direct vs switched, except toasts, announcements and status lines, which D-389 allows. Code: hud.gd:92-103 `func _refresh_texts() ... if not _frozen: _refresh_all()`."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "godot/i18n/common.csv",
    "description": "The msgid '{name} · {hp} PV' (and its translations) uses a normal space between the HP number and its unit, while '{value} PV' uses a no-break space (D-198 typography). On the hunt cards at 1280x720 the line breaks between the number and the unit: « Petit titan des marais · 400 » / « PV » in French, and « 400 » / « ОЗ » in Russian. Other msgids with units have the same plain space: '{hp} / {max_hp} PV', '{damage} PV ({percent})', '{seconds} s', '{minutes} min {seconds} s'.",
    "evidence": "Windowed capture (Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64.exe, capture.gd --lang=ru --resolutions=1280x720) %TEMP%/lht-review-i18n-w4/shots/ru/combat_launch_hunts_1280x720.png: the hunt card title wraps with « ОЗ » alone on the second line. The integration agent's own %TEMP%/lht-v1-w4-i18n-integration/shots/fr/combat_launch_hunts_1280x720.png shows « 400 » / « PV » split the same way. CSV bytes (Python repr): common.csv '{value}\\xa0PV' has an NBSP, but '{name} · {hp} PV' and its ru translation '{name} · {hp} ОЗ' have a plain U+0020."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "lens": "plan",
  "issues": [
   {
    "severity": "medium",
    "file": "godot/tests/e2e/journey/journey.gd",
    "description": "The §50 journey E2E (`dev.ps1 journey`) does not fix its language. Run tests are pinned to fr (D-388), but the journey profile has no `language` field, so it takes the OS language. Several of its checks compare text that code wrote through Tx (Labels with auto_translate DISABLED, or status texts) against French msgids. On any machine whose OS language is not French, the acceptance journey fails at step 3. It passes here only because this machine is fr-FR. The last journey run was after wave 5.1, so it has never run against the extracted texts on a non-French system.",
    "evidence": "journey.gd:234 `connection.text.contains(\"En ligne\")`: main_menu.gd:96 writes `Tx.t(\"En ligne\")`, which shell.csv gives as \"Online\" in en. journey.gd:427 `status_text == \"Disposition enregistrée.\"` (en \"Layout saved.\"). journey.gd:483/490 compare `_band_title`/`card.title_text()` with WorldText.APPROACH_TITLE/APPROACH_SHORT, the raw msgids, while the card shows Tx text (en \"Titan approaching\"). journey.gd:634 looks for \"+%s or\". `grep pin_system_language` finds no call under tests/e2e: it is set only in run_tests.gd:41, a few unit tests and capture.gd. This machine is fr-FR (Get-Culture), which hides the problem. Possible fix: pin fr in the journey (LhtLocale.pin_system_language + apply), or write `language: fr` into its profile, or compare against Tx.t(msgid)."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "docs/v1/STATUS.md",
    "description": "The plan's final check list has not been run on v1 + wave 4. The E2E runs named in the plan (`layout_during_combat`, `double_spend`, `real_server_village`, `journey`, `real_server_perf`) were last run after wave 5.1 (242a384). They were not run after 5.2 (combat-free-view, held spending), after 5.3 (text extraction), or on this integration branch. STATUS still lists 'revue finale et E2E' as left for 5.4, and the integration report does not mention them.",
    "evidence": "STATUS.md:700 'E2E contre le vrai serveur sur `v1` après la vague 5.1 (`242a384`…)'. STATUS.md:727 'Reste (5.4) : … revue finale et E2E.' Plan nifty-rolling-crane.md 'Vérification': 'e2e `layout_during_combat`, `double_spend`, `real_server_village`, `journey` ; `real_server_perf`'. The integration report lists only run_tests, lint and art checks."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "README.md",
    "description": "The root README still describes the removed construction system and says nothing about languages. It advertises 'constructions à minuteur', says the server runs a background task for constructions, and says the dev console has 'constructions terminées'. All of these were removed by D-369. The 9-language client and the 'Langue' setting (D-382..D-386) are not mentioned in README.md or godot/README.md.",
    "evidence": "README.md:8 '**village** : … Temple (codex), constructions à minuteur.' README.md:38 '…mène les tâches de fond (cycle du titan mondial, constructions)'. README.md:148 console 'délais' row: '…; constructions terminées ; …'. `git grep -iE 'i18n|traduction|langue' README.md godot/README.md` finds nothing. README.md is unchanged in c9ca01c..HEAD."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "godot/core/village/village_text.gd",
    "description": "Dead code left from the construction timer. `VillageText.FINISHING` (\"Finalisation…\", the D-242 'construction échue' text) and the `READY_IN` defaults of `VillageText.countdown` / `BuildingPanel.add_countdown` can no longer be reached from the game: the only caller passes its own prefix and done text. The msgids \"Finalisation…\" and \"Prêt dans {time}\" are still translated into 8 languages for nothing. `common.csv` also keeps the unused msgid \"{value} PV\". STATUS 5.1 already flagged FINISHING as unreachable.",
    "evidence": "village_text.gd:37 `const FINISHING := \"Finalisation…\"`, :118 `countdown(..., template = READY_IN, done_text = FINISHING)`. building_panel.gd:22 duplicates `READY_IN`, :290 `add_countdown(..., prefix = READY_IN, done_text = VillageText.FINISHING ...)`. The only callers are merchant_panel.gd:130 and chest_offer.gd:132, and both pass COOLDOWN_PREFIX and VillageText.ALMOST. Only test_village_rules.gd:137 reaches 'Finalisation…'. Scanning the game code (core, scenes, .tscn) for each CSV msgid leaves '{value} PV' (common.csv) unused."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "serveur/internal/layout/dev.go",
    "description": "Two stale texts flagged in the 5.1 reviews are still there. The dev console help for automatic placement says 'jusqu'à la capacité', but placement now stops at `Slots(grid)` and every V1 grid is unlimited (D-371). The API header of ArtBuildingView documents a 3-argument `model_for_state(id, state, level)`, but the function takes 2 arguments (D-370).",
    "evidence": "layout/dev.go:81 Help: \"Les tours les plus rares, jusqu'à la capacité, en murs successifs…\" while dev.go:173 uses `Arrange(grid, min(len(towers), Slots(grid)))`. godot/art/village/art_building_view.gd:20 '##   ArtBuildingView.model_for_state(id, state, level) -> model file' vs :58 `static func model_for_state(id: StringName, building_state: StringName) -> String`. STATUS.md 5.1 'Limites connues' lists both as open."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "docs/v1/DECISIONS.md",
    "description": "docs/v1 does not yet reflect wave 4. This is the orchestrator's merge step, but today the docs and the code disagree. D-385 still gives the fire-rate unit msgid as « {value} tir/s », while the code and CSV now use a plural msgid. The STATUS 'Langues' row still says '🟡 socle seulement', and its 5.4 line lists the live-switch test, the no-French test and the captures as still to do. The capture `--lang` option is missing from PLAN.md and godot/README.md. D-391..D-396, which the integration agent asked for, are not there.",
    "evidence": "DECISIONS.md:335 (D-385) 'Unités en msgids à espace insécable (« {value} s », « {value} tir/s », …)' vs stat_format.gd:23 `const RATE_TEXT := \"{value} tir/s|{value} tir/s\"` and common.csv:17. STATUS.md:667 'Langues | 🟡 socle seulement'; STATUS.md:727 'Reste (5.4) : bascule à chaud…'. PLAN.md:183 and godot/README.md:160 give the capture command without `--lang`. `grep D-39[1-6] docs/v1/DECISIONS.md` finds nothing."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "lens": "translations",
  "issues": [
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "godot/i18n/combat.csv",
    "description": "The same sentence about the world titan's last hit is translated two different ways in es, de, ko and pt. The two French msgids differ only by the space before \"!\": combat_summary.gd:230 uses a normal space, world_text.gd:82 uses U+00A0. So they are two msgids, and the battle report says it one way while the world banner says it another way for the same event. The de row in combat.csv also puts {titan} in the dative (\"Du hast {titan} den Todesstoß versetzt!\"), which i18n_style.md forbids for de. Fix: use the world.csv:27 wording in combat.csv:73: es \"¡Con tu golpe final cae {titan}!\", de \"Durch deinen Todesstoß fällt {titan}!\", pt \"Com seu golpe final, cai {titan}!\". Pick one ko wording for both rows; \"결정타를 날려 {titan} 처치에 성공했습니다!\" avoids 당신. A cleaner fix is to give combat_summary.gd:230 the NBSP msgid so only one row remains.",
    "evidence": "combat.csv:73 \"Vous avez porté le coup fatal à {titan} !\" (normal space) → es \"¡Diste el golpe final a {titan}!\", de \"Du hast {titan} den Todesstoß versetzt!\", ko \"결정타를 날려 {titan} 처치에 성공했습니다!\", pt \"Você deu o golpe final em {titan}!\". world.csv:27 \"Vous avez porté le coup fatal à {titan} !\" → es \"¡Con tu golpe final cae {titan}!\", de \"Durch deinen Todesstoß fällt {titan}!\", ko \"당신이 결정타를 날렸습니다: {titan}!\", pt \"Com seu golpe final, cai {titan}!\". In the source, combat_summary.gd:230 has a plain space and world_text.gd:82 has M-BM- (NBSP), checked with cat -A."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "godot/i18n/common.csv",
    "description": "The German duration formatter uses two minute abbreviations. Row 21 writes \"min\" (\"5 min 30 s\"), while row 22, row 67 and world.csv:39 write \"Min.\" (\"1 Std. 05 Min.\", \"5 Min.\", \"vor 5 Min.\"). The same countdown or cooldown can therefore show \"min\" or \"Min.\" depending on its length. Fix: common.csv:21 de → \"{minutes} Min. {seconds} s\".",
    "evidence": "common.csv:21 de \"{minutes} min {seconds} s\"; common.csv:22 de \"{hours} Std. {minutes} Min.\"; common.csv:67 de \"{minutes} Min.\"; world.csv:39 de \"vor {n} Min.\". The four rows are chosen by VillageText/StatFormat duration helpers depending on the value."
   },
   {
    "severity": "low",
    "file": "godot/i18n/world.csv",
    "description": "The ru line under the world-titan panel's state is about 1.8 times the French length (18 → 32 characters before the name). It is a label line, the killer name can be up to 32 wide characters, and the banner title already says the titan is down. Fix: world.csv:37 ru → \"Добивающий удар: {killer}\". This keeps the glossary term and drops the verb.",
    "evidence": "world.csv:37 \"Coup fatal de {killer}\" → ru \"Добивающий удар нанёс игрок {killer}\". Measured width ratio is 32/18 (script $TEMP/lht-review-translation

