# Design — main menu camp (1) and LHT1 pixel-art hunt titans option (2)

## 1. Main menu camp (branch v1-w6-menu-camp)
User decision: a camp in the foreground of the first menu: a few trees, a banner/flag, a campfire; wind sways trees and banner; fire crackles with smoke; clouds drift visibly.
- All current .glb came from the archived procedural kit (godot/legacy/procedural_art/tools/export_models.gd via model_families.gd) — the README documents it as the way to regenerate models. Reused meshes: trees (valley/vegetation/*.res), smoke (fx/meshes/puff.res), sparks (ember.res). Logs, stone ring, pole, cloth, ledge don't exist separately and primitive meshes have no vertex colours → one new file.
- New builder legacy/procedural_art/scenes/legacy_camp_builder.gd, exported by _export_sky() as assets/models/sky/camp.glb (root Camp): Ground (lit: rock ledge, grass top, logs, stone ring, pole); Trees (role foliage: 3–4 pine/broadleaf from ArtVegetation merged; vertex alpha = sway weight ((y-base)/height)^1.5 computed from position so split vertices stay identical); Banner (role cloth, from ArtOrnaments.banner, alpha 0 at pole → 1 at free edge); Fire (flame, tongues from ArtPrims.flame); markers FirePoint, SmokePoint.
- Outcrop: _build_outcrop loses its static banner pole; its 7 pines move to a new OutcropTrees node (foliage) — no static trees/flags next to swaying ones.
- New material roles foliage and cloth: add to ROLES in addons/lht_models/model_import.gd and model_writer.gd, and to ALPHA_ROLES (keep vertex alpha). foliage(), cloth() and shared_materials() in art/meshkit/art_materials.gd; files art/materials/foliage.tres, cloth.tres, one shader.
- art/shaders/wind.gdshader (lit; cull_back for foliage, cull_disabled for cloth):
```
uniform vec3 wind_direction = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.25); uniform float sway_amplitude; // m at weight 1
uniform float sway_speed; uniform float gust_speed; uniform float ripple_amplitude; uniform float ripple_speed; uniform float ripple_wavelength;
void vertex() {
  float w = COLOR.a; vec3 wp = (MODEL_MATRIX * vec4(VERTEX, 1.0)).xyz;
  float ph = dot(wp.xz, vec2(0.031, 0.047));
  float gust = 0.6 + 0.4 * sin(TIME * gust_speed + ph * 0.3);
  vec3 d = normalize(vec3(wind_direction.x, 0.0, wind_direction.z));
  vec3 off = d * sway_amplitude * w * w * gust * (0.7 + 0.3 * sin(TIME * sway_speed + ph));
  off += cross(d, vec3(0, 1, 0)) * ripple_amplitude * w * sin(TIME * ripple_speed - dot(wp, d) / ripple_wavelength);
  VERTEX += (inverse(mat3(MODEL_MATRIX)) * off);
  COLOR.rgb = srgb_to_linear(COLOR.rgb);
}
void fragment() { ALBEDO = COLOR.rgb; ROUGHNESS = 0.9; SPECULAR = 0.22; }
```
- Cloud drift: two instance uniforms in cloud.gdshader: drift (vec3 m/s) and drift_span; each puff's instance origin moves by drift*TIME wrapped within drift_span, puffs shrink to zero near wrap edges (no pop). Defaults 0 → valley clouds unchanged. CloudBanks get a slow drift; new DriftClouds MultiMesh (art/scenes/instances/drift_clouds.res, ~30 puffs at 300–900 m) visibly moves in the same +x wind.
- art/scenes/sky_backdrop.tscn: Camp node (instance of camp.glb) bottom-right; new art/fx/campfire.tscn at FirePoint: Embers CPUParticles3D (ember.res, particle material, irregular bursts), smoke.tscn instance with menu-scale overrides (puffs ~6×, velocities ~5×, gravity bent +x), OmniLight3D without shadows, AnimationPlayer autoplay looping a flicker of light energy (no script).
- Framing: keep MENU_EYE and DESCENT_*; the dive heads for screen point (0.58, 1.0) at 16:9, outcrop off-screen at 4:3 → camp bottom-right ~NDC (+0.5, −0.65) at 16:9, ~90–110 m from camera, trees ~20–25 m tall. Boot screen uses the same Backdrop. Cost: 4–5 draw calls, ~30 particles, 1 light.
- art/tests/check_backdrop.gd: camp nodes exist & use shared foliage/cloth materials; tree alpha < 0.1 at base, > 0.8 at top; banner alpha 0 at pole; at 16:9, 21:9, 4:3 the fire point projects inside the viewport, in the lower 40%, outside the menu panel rect; sampled set_descent(t) keeps the camera ≥ 25 m from the Camp AABB; DriftClouds has non-zero drift; geometry budget 20 → 24; check_meshkit covers new materials.
- Captures (godot/tools/capture/shots/menu.json): add a camp view (ArtSkyBackdrop.capture_set_view + tests/scenes/menu/menu_capture_stage.gd), shots menu_camp_1920x1080 and menu_wind_b_1920x1080 (wait_frames 150) to show motion; review all 14 existing shots (menu_* in 4 ratios, menu_boot, descent_1..4) — windowed, READ the PNGs.
- godot/README.md "Modèles 3D": document roles foliage/cloth, wind, camp.glb from the archived kit.

## 2. LHT1 pixel-art hunt titans option (branch v1-w6-lht1-hunt-sprites — WAVE 6.2, not 6.1)
(kept here for reference; implemented later)
- @abstract class_name ArtTitanActor extends Node3D (art/titan/art_titan_actor.gd): signals death_finished, escape_finished; abstract play_walk, set_facing, play_hit, play_death, play_escape, reset_pose, set_status, is_status_active, get_hit_point, get_height, is_dead, size_scale. ArtTitanView extends it; presenter _titan/titan_view() typed ArtTitanActor.
- art/titan/titan_sprite_view.tscn + art_titan_sprite_view.gd, create(skin, visual): %Sprite AnimatedSprite3D (billboard, nearest, shaded=false, alpha_cut OPAQUE_PREPASS, no shadow), %Footing (ArtTitanView.footing_mesh() made public), %PickBody, dust.tscn. Size = ArtTitanView.size_for(scale); pixel_size = UNIT_HEIGHT(7 m const on ArtTitanView) * skin.height_factor / skin.content_px; ground pivot offset.y from skin.foot_px (all frames of a skin same size); facing flip_h from dir·camera.right > 0 with ±0.15 dead zone (LHT1 sprites face left); walk speed_scale clamp(speed/ref_speed, 0.5, 2), speed 0 pauses frame 0; hit: modulate reddish + 0.15 m recoil; slow: icy modulate + frost ring; burn: existing burn effect scaled (0.6,1,0.6); death anim once + 0.8 s fade → death_finished; escape: frost tint, squash (0.05,1.6) → escape_finished; detached view finishes at once; hit point 0.55 of height.
- Assets: copy 9 PNG to assets/sprites/lht1/{goblin,dunkey,golem}/{walk,attack,death}.png (never reference lht_titans_extract); imports pinned compress/mode=0, no mipmaps, detect_3d/compress_to=0; art/titan/lht1/{goblin,dunkey,golem}_frames.tres from monster_skin_5, _7 and monster_skin SpriteFrames (walk loop 7–8 fps, attack 10 fps, death once 5–6 fps; even out golem frame heights).
- Table art/titan/lht1/lht1_hunt_skins.tres (ArtTitanSpriteSkins/ArtTitanSpriteSkin): by_titan hunt_01 → goblin, hunt_02 → dunkey, hunt_03 → golem; by_variant fallback golem/crystal/ancient → golem, horned → dunkey (fixtures use hunt_tiny, hunt_marsh).
- ProfileSettings.hunt_titan_style "3d"/"lht1" default "3d"; settings panel "Combat" section "Titans de chasse" with toggles %HuntTitans3D / %HuntTitansLht1 (texts "3D", "LHT1" untranslated); CombatPresenter.lht1_hunt_sprites set by combat_module from Session.settings before setup(); kind=="hunt" → sprite view; combat_preview.gd and titan_preview.gd accept option "lht1": true.
- Tests: test_combat_presenter (hunt+option → sprite view; MSQ & default stay 3D; position/death/escape/status/show_end on sprite view), art/tests/check_titan_sprites.gd, ProfileSettings round trip, settings toggle saves, test_code_rules: no res://lht_titans_extract reference. Captures combat.json combat_fight_lht1_*, combat_escape_lht1; titans.json titan_hunt_0{1,2,3}_lht1; re-check menu_settings_1280x720.
- Decisions: exception to D-032 (opt-in), ArtTitanActor, mapping; README third-party note.

